{
  "sn22.59:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.59 ",
  "sn22.59:0.2": "6. Involvement ",
  "sn22.59:0.3": "The Characteristic of Not-Self ",
  "sn22.59:1.1": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Varanasi in the deer park at Isipatana. ",
  "sn22.59:1.2": "There the Buddha addressed the group of five mendicants: ",
  "sn22.59:1.3": "“Mendicants!” ",
  "sn22.59:1.4": "“Venerable sir,” they replied. ",
  "sn22.59:1.5": "The Buddha said this: ",
  "sn22.59:2.1": "“Mendicants, form is not-self. ",
  "sn22.59:2.2": "For if form were self, it wouldn’t lead to affliction. And you could compel form: ",
  "sn22.59:2.3": "‘May my form be like this! May it not be like that!’ ",
  "sn22.59:2.4": "But because form is not-self, it leads to affliction. And you can’t compel form: ",
  "sn22.59:2.5": "‘May my form be like this! May it not be like that!’ ",
  "sn22.59:3.1": "Feeling is not-self … ",
  "sn22.59:3.2": "",
  "sn22.59:3.3": "",
  "sn22.59:3.4": "",
  "sn22.59:3.5": "",
  "sn22.59:4.1": "Perception is not-self … ",
  "sn22.59:4.2": "Choices are not-self … ",
  "sn22.59:4.3": "",
  "sn22.59:4.4": "",
  "sn22.59:4.5": "",
  "sn22.59:4.6": "",
  "sn22.59:5.1": "Consciousness is not-self. ",
  "sn22.59:5.2": "For if consciousness were self, it wouldn’t lead to affliction. And you could compel consciousness: ",
  "sn22.59:5.3": "‘May my consciousness be like this! May it not be like that!’ ",
  "sn22.59:5.4": "But because consciousness is not-self, it leads to affliction. And you can’t com